    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615-a5">

                <pb facs="0930" n="802" xml:id="pg802"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 209.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The director of the local
                            police to the central department of police,
                            Neuchátet</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chaux-de-fonds</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 24,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: To carry out the instructions of your
                    dispatch of the 22d instant concerning Henry Theodore Christian Emeis, I sent
                    for this amateur to come to my office and communicated to him your decision.
                    After some hesitation he declared that he had not been at Davos for some years
                    past, and, moreover, that he was no longer a German, but an American citizen,
                    and finally produced the passport, which I herewith inclose, and which you will
                    kindly return.</p>
                <p>Regarding the observations which I have made on the subject of his first and
                    second statements, he replied that he did not think that one would be so
                    exacting, that he had not understood me well, and other such more or less
                    evasive remarks.</p>
                <p>Believe me, &amp;c.,</p>
                <p>The director of the local police,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRITZ ROBERT DUCOMMUN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
